{
  "info": {
    "name": "Fonchys Minimarket - API REST",
    "description": "Pruebas de la API REST. Ejecutar 1a (obtener CSRF), 1b (iniciar sesion) y 2 (consultar productos) en orden. El token se guarda automaticamente y Postman conserva la cookie JSESSIONID. Mantener habilitado el cookie jar. Las peticiones posteriores crean, modifican y desactivan datos de prueba. Consultar postman/README.md.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "baseUrl", "value": "http://localhost:8080" },
    { "key": "loginEmail", "value": "admin@fonchys.com" },
    { "key": "loginPassword", "value": "admin123" },
    { "key": "fonchysCsrfToken", "value": "" },
    { "key": "productoId", "value": "" }
  ],
  "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1a. GET /login (obtener CSRF)",
      "protocolProfileBehavior": { "followRedirects": false },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "prerequest",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.collectionVariables.unset('fonchysCsrfToken');"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Formulario disponible (200)', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "const input = pm.response.text().match(/<input\\b[^>]*\\bname=[\"']_csrf[\"'][^>]*>/i);",
              "const token = input && input[0].match(/\\bvalue=[\"']([^\"']+)[\"']/i);",
              "pm.test('El formulario contiene un token CSRF', () => pm.expect(token, 'Borra las cookies de localhost y repite 1a').to.not.be.null);",
              "if (pm.response.code === 200 && token) {",
              "  pm.collectionVariables.set('fonchysCsrfToken', token[1]);",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "url": "{{baseUrl}}/login",
        "description": "Devuelve HTML deliberadamente para obtener el token CSRF. El script guarda el token y el cookie jar conserva la sesion. Despues ejecuta 1b. Si venias usando cookies antiguas, borra las de localhost antes de este paso."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "1b. POST /login (iniciar sesion admin)",
      "protocolProfileBehavior": { "followRedirects": false },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Login responde con redireccion (302)', () => pm.response.to.have.status(302));",
              "pm.test('Administrador autenticado: destino /dashboard', () => {",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('Location'), 'Si apunta a /login, revisa CSRF y cookies; si contiene error=true, revisa las credenciales').to.match(/\\/dashboard$/);",
              "});",
              "pm.collectionVariables.unset('fonchysCsrfToken');"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "{{baseUrl}}/login",
        "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/x-www-form-urlencoded" }],
        "body": {
          "mode": "urlencoded",
          "urlencoded": [
            { "key": "username", "value": "{{loginEmail}}", "type": "text" },
            { "key": "password", "value": "{{loginPassword}}", "type": "text" },
            { "key": "_csrf", "value": "{{fonchysCsrfToken}}", "type": "text" }
          ]
        },
        "description": "Ejecutar inmediatamente despues de 1a, conservando las cookies. Para admin se espera 302 hacia /dashboard; /login no devuelve JSON. Postman guarda automaticamente el nuevo JSESSIONID. Cada nuevo intento de login debe empezar por 1a."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "2. GET /api/productos (200)",
      "protocolProfileBehavior": { "followRedirects": false },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "pm.test('Content-Type JSON', () => pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('Content-Type')).to.include('application/json'));",
              "pm.test('Devuelve un arreglo', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json()).to.be.an('array'));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [{ "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" }],
        "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/productos"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "3. POST /api/productos (201)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Status 201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
              "pm.test('Tiene header Location', () => pm.response.headers.has('Location'));",
              "const body = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('productoId', body.id);",
              "pm.test('Devuelve el id generado', () => pm.expect(body.id).to.be.a('number'));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
        "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/productos",
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"nombre\": \"Producto Demo Postman\",\n  \"precio\": 5.90,\n  \"stock\": 30\n}"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "4. GET /api/productos/{id} (200)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "pm.test('Es el producto creado', () => pm.response.json().id == pm.collectionVariables.get('productoId'));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/productos/{{productoId}}"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "5. PUT /api/productos/{id} (200)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "pm.test('Nombre actualizado', () => pm.response.json().nombre === 'Producto Demo Postman (editado)');"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "PUT",
        "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
        "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/productos/{{productoId}}",
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"nombre\": \"Producto Demo Postman (editado)\",\n  \"precio\": 6.50,\n  \"stock\": 25\n}"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "6. DELETE /api/productos/{id} (204)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Status 204 No Content', () => pm.response.to.have.status(204));",
              "pm.test('Sin body', () => pm.response.text() === '');"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "DELETE",
        "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/productos/{{productoId}}"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "7. GET /api/productos/999999 (404 - no encontrado)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Status 404', () => pm.response.to.have.status(404));",
              "pm.test('Cuerpo con mensaje de error', () => pm.response.json().message.includes('no encontrado'));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/productos/999999"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "8. POST /api/productos invalido (400 - validacion)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Status 400', () => pm.response.to.have.status(400));",
              "pm.test('Cuerpo con status y message', () => {",
              "  const b = pm.response.json();",
              "  pm.expect(b.status).to.eql(400);",
              "  pm.expect(b.message).to.be.a('string');",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
        "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/productos",
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"nombre\": \"\",\n  \"precio\": -1,\n  \"stock\": -5\n}"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "9. POST /api/ventas invalido (400 - carrito vacio)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Status 400', () => pm.response.to.have.status(400));",
              "pm.test('Mensaje menciona el carrito', () => pm.response.json().message.toLowerCase().includes('producto'));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
        "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/ventas",
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"items\": []\n}"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "10. POST /api/ventas valido (201)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Status 201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
              "pm.test('Descuenta stock y calcula total', () => pm.response.json().total > 0);"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
        "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/ventas",
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"items\": [ { \"productoId\": 1, \"cantidad\": 1 } ],\n  \"clienteNombre\": \"Cliente Postman\"\n}"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
